   "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs` lower/1: Validate lowering inputs\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Reject unverified/stale IR and incompatible profiles/features; expose explicit supported-operation and target matrices. P5: admit SIMD/intrinsics only with declared target features, numeric mode and alignment/layout evidence plus a valid fallback or rejection. A target wrapper does not justify unchecked intrinsics or change source legality; guarded variant selection and target lowering remain distinct interfaces. Criterion profile-gap/native/feature-guard (Open): Input: Native SIMD/intrinsic lowering or shipped variant with declared feature, numeric semantics, alignment/layout, portable wrapper or target namespace and fallback/rejection policy. Accept: Check feature-specific lowering eligibility and separately select a shipped variant only under guards matching target/numeric/layout assumptions; retain a valid fallback or explicit rejection. Unchecked intrinsics remain unsafe. Reject: Missing/unavailable target feature, implicit backend numeric behavior, unsupported alignment/layout, invalid guarded variant/fallback or unchecked intrinsic presented as safe. Required outputs: SIMD/target feature and numeric/layout/guard report, eligible/ineligible target and fallback fixtures, P5-SIMD/NUMERIC or lowering diagnostic with feature/provider/proof/origin context. Dependencies: backend-interface, opt/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/opt2-implement-structural-families, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping native/feature-guard; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.",
