   "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup` Finish managed/native execution, startup, panic and cleanup\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Development evaluator](../../bootstrap/gravity/src/gravity/runtime.gravity) and [native manifest](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/foundation/00287-minimal-native-runtime-manifest.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Executed startup/failure/resource fixtures and manifest-to-service agreement; before user code, validate selected provider existence, artifact versions, grant scopes, compiled contracts, profile/target compatibility and enabled safety/audit requirements; reject a missing required provider unless a declared fallback applies, with positive fallback and negative mismatch fixtures under [L15 runtime providers](../../docs/phase-01-core-language/025-l15-capability-provider-specification.md) . R1/R3/R4: typed host adapters with effects, capabilities, taint, error and source-map contracts; selected host/version/module/collection/dynamic-state manifests; startup, initialization, handoff and teardown order; explicit panic/trap/abort/unwind/result policy; host null/undefined conversion, exception and rejected-promise translation; Gravity equality/hashing/serialization conformance; deterministic linear cleanup independent of process exit or GC. Reject undeclared helper effects, untranslated/null foreign values and GC-only linear cleanup; debug services must be absent or release-policy marked. Dependencies: Lower supplies ABI and source maps, Legality supplies legal services, and Auth supplies grants; selected compiler services do not close all managed/native targets. P4: execute deterministic cleanup for linear host resources despite GC; managed objects remain GC-managed and only an explicit boundary can rely on finalizer timing. Reject GC-only cleanup where deterministic release is required; preserve exactly-once flow evidence from Legality separately from executed terminal operations. Translate host errors through the declared Gravity failure channel with source/generated origins. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/deterministic-resource-cleanup (Open): Input: Hosted managed objects and linear file/socket/lock/transaction resources under declared rooting/finalizer and Gravity cleanup contracts. Accept: Check exactly-once linear resource flow and separately execute required deterministic terminal cleanup despite host GC; permit managed object lifetime and explicit boundary finalizer behavior without turning all objects into linear resources. Reject: GC-only release for resources requiring deterministic cleanup, missing/double terminal operations, invalid failure-path ownership transfer and reliance on unspecified finalizer timing. Required outputs: Resource-flow and executed cleanup records for success/failure/transfer, host-boundary lifecycle metadata and P4-RESOURCE origin/effect/grant/host-policy diagnostics. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/deterministic-resource-cleanup; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.",
