   "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries` Implement memory, concurrency and typed FFI boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. Execute the [SAFE2-SAFE8 contracts](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md): declared allocation and cleanup failures, partial initialization cleanup, region/arena generation and borrow checks, release through the correct allocator/provider, callback lifetime/thread/reentrancy/release and foreign error/exception/promise translation. Reject retained borrows, post-reset access, missing FFI declarations, unsupported atomics and unsynchronized mutable access; validate immutable sharing, lock cleanup, actor/channel transfer and declared backpressure/cancellation. Inspect actual checks and audit records, with no hidden GC or host-thread fallback. . R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety. P4/P5: host-object/native FFI records bind runtime/version/symbol, Gravity and foreign types, rooting/ownership/lifetime, nullability, failure mapping, affinity, ABI, effects/grants and safe wrappers. Insufficient host metadata permits opaque provider-only handles, not unrestricted manipulation; raw native imports are not directly safe-callable. Exercise positive boundaries and missing metadata, ungranted call, invalid lifetime and untranslated failure rejection. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/typed-object-boundary (Open): Input: Host object boundary with runtime/version, symbol/class/module/member, Gravity/host type, rooting/ownership/lifetime, exception translation, affinity, effects/grants and source-map support. Accept: Emit and validate typed schema/protocol/foreign-handle boundaries before manipulation; insufficient metadata yields opaque values operated only through declared provider APIs. Reject: Untyped host object use, missing lifecycle/affinity/grant metadata and unnormalized host failures crossing into Gravity. Required outputs: Host interop/object/runtime dependency and deployment-capability manifests, typed-versus-opaque boundary fixtures, P4-HOST-OBJECT/EXCEPTION/CROSS-IMPORT and effect/grant diagnostics. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, schema, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/typed-object-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/native/ffi-boundary (Open): Input: Native foreign import/call with ABI/calling convention, link symbol, type mapping, ownership transfer/lifetime/nullability, failure/affinity, effects/grants and safe-wrapper or unsafe contract. Accept: Validate the complete foreign boundary, execute the admitted call through the wrapper, and separately translate declared foreign failures into Gravity; preserve ABI/source/provider identity and every safe-wrapper precondition. Reject: Raw import called directly from safe code, incomplete ABI/ownership/error metadata, missing grant, invalid lifetime/nullability/affinity and untranslated failure or unaudited raw memory. Required outputs: Native ABI/FFI/safety manifests and admitted/rejected call/failure fixtures with P5-FFI/RAW-MEMORY diagnostics identifying ABI/provider/effect/grant/source/generated origin. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping native/ffi-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.",
