    :criterion-id "profile-gap/hardware/capability-representation",
    :acceptance-text
    "Criterion profile-gap/hardware/capability-representation (Open): Input: Capability-hardware target manifest and typed pointer operation with word/address widths, bounds/granularity, provenance/derivation, permission bits, tag/seal/object/entry metadata. Accept: Select hardware capabilities only through the target manifest; type/layout-check representation and derivations for preserved provenance, enforced bounds and non-widening permissions. A conditional audited hardware authority boundary must retain its explicit preconditions and evidence. Reject: Pointers treated as integers, fabricated provenance, undeclared integer round-trip, unsupported representation or unchecked bounds/permission widening. Required outputs: Capability pointer/layout/metadata target manifest, legal derivation and rejected widening/representation fixtures, P8-CAPABILITY diagnostics identifying metadata field, module/signal/origin and target evidence. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/capability-representation; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.",
